Z||000000||swoods||08-07-2001||04:24 PM|||| Im been doing alot of reading on 2.5 and have seen alot of performance stuff but I would like info from all you 2.5 owners of what youve done to yours and whats worked best for that little Iron Duke.||||reg||14
Z||000001||StuGood||08-07-2001||05:57 PM||||Well, I'm kind of a Duke Dunce, myself, but I own one '88 Duke 5-speed (with a slipping clutch).  Haven't done much with mine (it's a very back-burner item on my agenda), but for some reason, I want give the little Duke a chance.  See what I can do, for little or no cost, to improve its performance.<P>I intend to replace the clutch (okay, so that'll cost), clean up the engine and see how far a little bit of care and elbow grease can take it.  If nothing else, I'll learn something about "the Iron Duke experience."  Also, I am about to "inherit" a 1985 Duke Automatic with a blown engine - if I decide to nurse it back to life, I'll learn even more.<P>Needless to say, I'll be watching the replies to this topic!     ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Jncomutt||08-07-2001||06:01 PM||||Add stickers and Yellow paint!  That'll sure add more HP.  Well according to those import guys...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I added a MSD coil, 6A, Wires, K&N a/f,   runs a flat 17 in the 1/4mi.  Soon to be added are a set of headers, a cat remover pipe, and freeflow exhaust.  I know its not much of engine work, but hey, its and econo-coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||08-07-2001||07:39 PM||||I have an 84 SE and have installed a K&N filter, MSD 8226 coil, 6A system and Accell 8mm wires.  real happy with these as I can feel a stronger pull above 3000 rpms.  Also have a Fiero store short shifter, and steel clutch pedal.  Car has 205000 miles and is running great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||swoods||08-08-2001||01:35 AM||||Does anybody race there 4cly and if you do how do you guys do?||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||08-08-2001||07:30 AM||||I, too, am a proud 2.5 owner.  Since you have been "reading" a lot and know all this "performance" stuff that we 4 bangers obviously can't find (other than breathing and firing issues as K & N, sparking and exhaust systems), please provide your references.  We, too, would like to improve performance and are willing to read what you did.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=52558159&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fotofrank||08-08-2001||01:52 PM||||  I have installed :<BR>MSD6A, and GM blaster coil<BR>Free flow cat<BR>Hooker tri-Y header<BR>Holley input<BR>Holley TB<BR>K&N filter<BR> The car goes preety good. I can keep up with a 2.8 no problem.<BR>Visit my web site (see below)<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000007||TI_3VOM||08-08-2001||04:25 PM||||StuGood,<BR>   I'm in the same boat as you. While there are some performance products out there for the Iron Duke/Tech IV (just got to look long and hard for them), most are for the 84-86 incarnation of our 4 cylinder. 87-88 year Dukes had new heads, meaning new bolt patterns for both intake and exhaust manifolds (kiss those Hooker headers and Holley induction systems good-bye  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ), as well as the switch to DIS. <BR>   I would love to pump up my 4-cyl. Just gotta keep looking.||||reg||4
Z||000008||TI_3VOM||08-08-2001||04:31 PM||||Question to any NIFE members...<P>I was in you club for a while ('till work and school took up most of my time), and seem to remember there was a member who was a 4-cylinder guru. I think his name was "Chaba" (sorry for the misspelling). Is he still around (or perhaps reads the forum)?||||reg||5
Z||000009||theogre||08-08-2001||07:07 PM||||Just what you can or need to do depends what year motor it is. 87 & up motors don't take many parts available for the older versions.||||reg||1
Z||000010||MrFeeArrow||08-08-2001||08:49 PM||||Check out this site,.....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/Fiero2M4/IronDuke.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/Fiero2M4/IronDuke.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Posthumane||08-08-2001||09:25 PM||||There are plenty of mods available if you look hard enough. Try searching under 'super duty.' The duke block isn't strong enough to go the whole super duty way, but you can do some milder stuff to it. I can't remember the page, but there was a guy who was making a rally fiero with a 2.5, which he called the "super tech IV" because it was a cross between the tech 4 and super duty.<P>I personally haven't done any mods to my engine (have a hard enough time keeping it running properly), and I can run mid to low 19's at race city. One thing I did do though is buy a fire extinguisher.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||StuGood||08-09-2001||10:04 AM||||Excellent link, MrFeeArrow!  Just what I was looking for!<BR>"...for those that have more time and patience than money and just want to have a<BR>reliable, efficient, smooth running little 4-banger that gives them reasonable<BR>performance," describes Stu to a tee!||||reg||10
